    "marks": 3,
    "markingMode": "MANUAL",
    "stem": "Prove that $\\dfrac{1 + \\tan^2\\theta}{1 + \\cot^2\\theta} \\equiv \\tan^2\\theta$.",
    "answerSpec": {
     "markScheme": {
      "points": [
       {
        "id": "p1",
        "description": "M1 uses $1 + \\tan^2\\theta = \\sec^2\\theta$ and $1 + \\cot^2\\theta = \\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta$.",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p2",
        "description": "M1 writes $\\frac{\\sec^2\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}$.",
        "marks": 1
       },
       {
        "id": "p3",
        "description": "A1 concludes $= \\tan^2\\theta$.",
        "marks": 1
       }
      ]
     },
     "modelAnswer": "$$\n\\frac{1 + \\tan^2\\theta}{1 + \\cot^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\sec^2\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta} = \\frac{1/\\cos^2\\theta}{1/\\sin^2\\theta}\n$$\n\n$$\n= \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\tan^2\\theta\n$$"
    },
    "explanation": "Both brackets are Pythagorean identities."
   },
   {
